  "id": "RBI-COOLING-OFF",
  "title": "Digital loan: penal-free exit during cooling-off period",
  "obligation": "A borrower of a digital loan must be given an explicit option to exit by repaying the principal and proportionate APR without penalty during an initial cooling-off period fixed by the lender's Board (not less than one day); a reasonable one-time processing fee may be retained if disclosed upfront in the KFS.",
  "source": {
    "regulator": "RBI",
    "document": "Reserve Bank of India (Digital Lending) Directions, 2025",
    "reference": "RBI/2025-26/36 DOR.STR.REC.19/21.07.001/2025-26",
    "issue_date": "2025-05-08",
    "document_status": "in_force",
    "file": "regulations/rbi-lending-ai-governance/RBI_2025-05-08_digital-lending-directions-2025.md",
    "sha256": "f415a6c4ec53f90f5349446f59b401e8be7309a467008d98e0fce0ec0e4503b6",
    "text_basis": "native",
    "provenance": "official_html_extract",
    "locator": "Chapter III para 10(i) and 10(ii)",
    "quotes": [
      "The borrower shall be given an explicit option to exit a digital loan by paying the principal and the proportionate APR without any penalty during an initial “cooling-off period”.",
      "subject to the period so determined not being less than one day",
      "RE may retain a reasonable one-time processing fee, if the customer exits the loan during the cooling-off period. This, if applicable, shall be disclosed to the customer upfront in KFS."
    ],
    "url": "https://www.rbi.org.in/scripts/FS_Notification.aspx?Id=12848"
  },
  "check": {
